{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0069618a1905deb33c4a79b04f7b94e692c96adbd183f122581c028cddf9779a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4a34adc00dbe00effe11599c1adb71f0026577ed15c70f31c2972567167d753a","slc_cd6f8efbee49d81c80f30155e654411a7617333b8fcbe0f5ddb587dbef0d1b01","slc_f7f3d2310290422b96354177e0c770493e560dec805157decacdaa644f073158"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe","src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"Closing an issue is an explicit API mutation carrying a reason, message, typed evidence, and actor attribution; kata never infers closure from git history.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_00e40100e2d03306aae4a59f12b46d255a26fd1fb10d9dd744ec3f3b94cdeb7f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7d8eb9a34e805859fb7cea7b2d9e0f3c57887db6b8367d3c4facfcbc9caae89d","slc_cd6f8efbee49d81c80f30155e654411a7617333b8fcbe0f5ddb587dbef0d1b01"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe"],"text":"By default issue state lives in a local SQLite database under KATA_HOME; teams can opt into a remote daemon or federation, and a shared daemon can use Postgres via KATA_DSN.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_16169b53e2cc0e4832f4a8f9eee939ee0aa5b6f4c8d37ddc2a7e78cae1340972","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1d5141f08eb7ddbcc4f6978ce1aa54d90b6cc0ec6514a0459cefd27c449383cc","slc_5da49345e12910118af44d9c894d289fdc7245af03e244ef391c0fd35b54c83c"],"source_ids":["src_c2d21531c29051979a0326fc4156b243"],"text":"Clients auto-start a local daemon when none is reachable; an autostart_idle_timeout lets such a narrowly scoped daemon exit after foreground use stops, while explicit daemons remain long-running.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1d761045d120ea8923262dbdeef993672c801706f18f46f8bb703e82304d9a4b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_442c955dd7cbf0796049350f64daf5441373a59278ceb7c017fe06f6efa9f137","slc_b3a20587b1e0538665557753cc6e4a85418afbb80a869a78d37713ec57ecf6ff"],"source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"Every state change appends to an immutable event log with the actor recorded; actors are free-form snapshots on events, not foreign keys, and there is no global user registry.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_22c69789f13d00e4cc72b49dc5ad28928c01efea182316a37a049d6e99ab22d5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9ad0d5c8a434ab38435a2d79a718f94ade27e6c5670dbd62dccd219ecc6a9e3c","slc_cd6f8efbee49d81c80f30155e654411a7617333b8fcbe0f5ddb587dbef0d1b01"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe","src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"The CLI offers agent-oriented ergonomics: stable short refs, --json and --agent output, idempotent creates, semantic-aware search, a claim flow, and predictable failure modes.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2a93491b1c047b51d85a89b0e727b42c6a4d70169445e82ef1e16ead53e4c486","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6ded19ad812834fc6ee90adfbc71246d55346854f9c07fc2507da88e1245310a","slc_7d8eb9a34e805859fb7cea7b2d9e0f3c57887db6b8367d3c4facfcbc9caae89d"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe","src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"All reads and writes go through kata's HTTP API; no client opens SQLite or Postgres directly, and a Go app can mount the listener-free service in-process.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2cb762dd951f0df0bc2aa614f13ca8aa4c7feaf13a95ec1136cdf1683d910641","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e9c0eccac019a0d3089aadfaa997233ada6dd8c5c9438b659f31dbb7b601ed1c"],"source_ids":["src_c2d21531c29051979a0326fc4156b243"],"text":"On an idle-enabled auto-start daemon, scheduled work is opportunistic: timers do not keep the process resident, so continuous sync, federation, timed claims, embeddings, or hooks need an explicit service-managed daemon.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2ea7f8f489d5b6ec35b8382ef7a8e28bf02a6179c72919e880d6269ccf334bea","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e5ec4f604e488adff9b277f38ab49ff883228e0661c4f217b4efdd98a5178b6","slc_7d8eb9a34e805859fb7cea7b2d9e0f3c57887db6b8367d3c4facfcbc9caae89d"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe"],"text":"kata is a durable task ledger for coding agents and humans: agents create, claim, relate, and close issues with evidence via CLI, while humans supervise in a terminal UI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3d3002806729950234aaffc9759ad092cfbd88ac69489d08cef8df52280d327b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_25abe0d2e116de1f9f243dde501f4ac97234ade4d98579d4ef49af6b80feb042"],"source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"Workspace identity derives from the normalized git remote URL rather than the filesystem path, so clones resolve to the same project; one git repository attaches to exactly one project.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3e3425fb2166eb68f9fdb901185b35e92b3106eab6b25f1057027a73901f37c1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_853b9e49b5be2a024291eabd41c360c06691672e5675ba62fdf702e0b55a58bc"],"source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"The surface is deliberately small: three relationship types, labels, owners, comments, and a constrained integer priority 0-4; there is no in_progress status, severity field, threaded replies, reactions, attachments, or markdown rendering.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4e78ed48a486b339474f3c80394ef7cb852392df2973ed88bd44f00e912a91e4","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_010d4e2a4ee75597d6e6b1b7f2d8be039169d388bc5d47766b021d0b6b9c7b10","slc_cd6f8efbee49d81c80f30155e654411a7617333b8fcbe0f5ddb587dbef0d1b01"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe","src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"kata uses pure-Go SQLite via modernc.org/sqlite with no CGO, a Huma-based HTTP API over a Unix socket, and claims no runtime dependencies beyond the single binary.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6535b61aee64a46d6b5d041021467c3238e8df80651fc688e233d709c10108e2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c9ae50c6c3bf852fb1a70f8efca8fb1e4d27b74fd71d3f26195c6d01a323b4d2"],"source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"Permanent non-goals include workspace-local behavior overrides, per-issue SSE subscriptions, bulk mutation endpoints, remote webhooks, and a (kata-#N) commit-message convention.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_668d7dd62c30f29502c922545840f93b4560fba604e36c08db8b26a90b460872","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_33a206a06f9972077f24fc0fa24981eb5a797feaa6ce4d7e11b844c6a5d63734","slc_737b8477b05664a1aadf77ef623d42acb3c46be42bec2b92e01c47445dd5eef8"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe"],"text":"kata init --with-agents writes a managed briefing into AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md without overwriting existing content, and --with-codex-hooks installs structured Codex SessionStart hooks in .codex/hooks.json.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7558ec539179c9b0b5fb17d46dba15625093c92aca35bbcbfbbfb1866c250621","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_95eaaeb42dfc1ecf63c77e3bfa20bc196b49eba290458cf307bac6e89bf40f73","slc_cd6f8efbee49d81c80f30155e654411a7617333b8fcbe0f5ddb587dbef0d1b01"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe","src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"The product ships as one Go binary with a CLI, a long-lived daemon, a TUI, and a browser UI served by the daemon with no separate backend.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7dbb4dd46e57259ad759c2c67680af5cc34dab6e9cfbd95fda4154a0cd21a92f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_084ff3d404f275eded50f1fe759e70ebf57b1913b0a2921db7bfff180ee96e16","slc_b8880c24f1714c05576ae535aa7d5e2c3c6599a7854e63da81d55fee81fe26f1"],"source_ids":["src_b7638ca697075274a0e1a3eb1157bafe"],"text":"kata is intentionally not a project-management suite, git workflow engine, agent worker pool, or SaaS tracker; it does not ride git remotes for sharing, relying on the remote daemon and federation instead.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_89e6452e8b4e8fd72736a2a91c39c87bf02b8a3ac5d94656580e0409a83deccc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bbf05df1606171a8bd499efd03af2522400b0d72c8f26074975afa99697a2bef"],"source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"The loopback HTTP server rejects non-empty Origin headers, requires application/json Content-Type on mutations, and emits no CORS headers to resist drive-by browser requests.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","created_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8c52c55eccbd5b2c6970defb70c71ad8b502d7ea2e24c19825928526eb60a8e3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"kenn-io/kata@f41a33383aba snapshot f7283538f30a32a1","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b46859e0174aa29d7b233b5cb40ab6763b06bd31d2937cfe84a4ca454ffed794","slc_bbf05df1606171a8bd499efd03af2522400b0d72c8f26074975afa99697a2bef"],"source_ids":["src_f8e530c979eb5711b2ebbde75659c344"],"text":"Local mode trusts the OS user with no authentication on a Unix socket or loopback listener; shared/remote modes require a bearer token and explicit trust opt-in before credentials cross a plaintext non-loopback connection.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:02:20Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4da85783a9e641e4b7f030e2fecda46f"}
